target:    uninstall.php
gate:      composer test:uninstall-data-safety
kind:      restore-defect
expect:    is gone on the KEEP-data path
rationale: Puts the strip behind the delete-data opt-in, at the call site that survives -- the one at the top of uninstall.php. This is the original defect, relocated: the credential is written into FREE's option array by Pro, and free deleted that array only when delete_data_on_uninstall was 'on', which defaults to 'no'. It replaces V8-credential-survives-keep-data-01, which pinned the same defect at a call site this commit removed as redundant -- that mutation SURVIVED a registry run for exactly that reason, and a mutation on dead code restores nothing. Deleting it without registering this would have retired the defect class rather than the duplicate.
---
--- a/uninstall.php
+++ b/uninstall.php
@@ -26,8 +26,10 @@
 // this matters for, the one whose external database is configured and gone. Everything after
 // that line, this file included, would simply not run. The handle is built from the LOCAL
 // $slimstat_options read above, so removing the stored copy first cannot break it.
-slimstat_uninstall_credentials();
-slimstat_uninstall_network_credentials();
+if ($slimstat_delete_data) {
+    slimstat_uninstall_credentials();
+    slimstat_uninstall_network_credentials();
+}
 
 // Every key the connection is opened from, so the list that BUILDS a handle and the list that
 // REMOVES it cannot drift. A fifth member — a port, a socket, a TLS path — added below and
